# Audiobookshelf + Traefik + Let's Encrypt — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in each value before `docker compose up`.
# `.env` is gitignored — never commit real credential values.
#
# Image versions are NOT set here. The tested tag + sha256 digest for every
# image lives in the compose file's `x-images` block, so `git pull` delivers
# the version combination this repository has tested. To pin a different
# version yourself, uncomment and set:
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_IMAGE_TAG=ghcr.io/advplyr/audiobookshelf:2.36.0@sha256:…

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Traefik reverse proxy
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Email address for Let's Encrypt renewal notices. REQUIRED.
TRAEFIK_ACME_EMAIL=admin@example.com

# Hostname for the Traefik dashboard (basic-auth protected). REQUIRED.
TRAEFIK_HOSTNAME=traefik.audiobookshelf.example.com

# Basic Authentication for the Traefik dashboard.
# Format: USERNAME:BCRYPT_HASH (with $ characters doubled to $$ for compose)
#     htpasswd -nbB traefikadmin YOUR_STRONG_PASSWORD | sed 's/\$/\$\$/g'
# REQUIRED — do not ship production without changing this.
TRAEFIK_BASIC_AUTH=change_me_generate_with_htpasswd_and_replace_this_string

# Log level: DEBUG, INFO, WARN, ERROR. Default: WARN.
# TRAEFIK_LOG_LEVEL=WARN

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Audiobookshelf
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public hostname. Must resolve to this server's public IP for the
# Let's Encrypt TLS-ALPN challenge. REQUIRED.
#
# Note that the application lives at https://<hostname>/audiobookshelf and not
# at the root; that path is compiled into its browser bundle and cannot be
# moved. Traefik redirects the bare hostname there, so you can hand out either.
AUDIOBOOKSHELF_HOSTNAME=books.example.com

# Where your audiobooks and podcasts actually live on this host. Mounted
# READ-WRITE, unlike the video and music templates in this fleet: Audiobookshelf
# downloads podcast episodes into the library and its file manager renames files
# to match fetched metadata. Read-only breaks both, silently.
# Defaults to ./audiobooks so the stack starts before you have decided.
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_LIBRARY_PATH=/mnt/storage/audiobooks

# There is no password to set here. The first account created through the web
# interface becomes the administrator, and until that happens the setup form is
# open to whoever reaches it.
# **Open the site and create your account immediately after deploy.**

# The uid/gid the server runs as, and which every file it writes into your
# library will belong to. Get them from the host with `id -u` and `id -g`, and
# make sure that user can read AND write the library directory.
#
# These are also what the init-permissions container gives the three volumes on
# first start, which is what lets the server run unprivileged at all.
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_UID=1000
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_GID=1000

# The port the server listens on inside the container. The image defaults to 80
# and expects to run as root; this template does not, and an unprivileged
# process cannot bind 80. Nothing is published to the host either way.
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_PORT=13378

# Timezone used for timestamps and scheduled tasks.
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_TZ=Etc/UTC

# How long Traefik will hold a single request or response open. Uploading an
# audiobook is one long request and the 60-second default for reading one is the
# ceiling people meet first, so this is 0. Raise the idle timeout instead if you
# want abandoned connections reaped sooner.
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_STREAM_TIMEOUT=0s
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_IDLE_TIMEOUT=600s
# Every Traefik template in this fleet also takes TRAEFIK_READ_TIMEOUT,
# TRAEFIK_WRITE_TIMEOUT and TRAEFIK_IDLE_TIMEOUT. When set they win over
# the names above, which keep working.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backups (defaults shown; override only to tune)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The archive covers /config: absdatabase.sqlite with users, libraries,
# listening progress, bookmarks, API tokens and podcast subscriptions. It does
# NOT cover your library, and it does not cover /metadata — covers and waveforms
# are rebuilt from the books, which is what keeps these archives small.
#
# TURN ON AUDIOBOOKSHELF'S OWN BACKUP SCHEDULE TOO (Settings -> Backups), with
# its path set to /backups. It is disabled in a fresh install. It exports the
# database consistently, where a tar copies the file while it is being written;
# pointing it at /backups puts its exports in the same directory these archives
# land in, under the same retention sweep.

# BACKUP_INIT_SLEEP=30m
# BACKUP_INTERVAL=24h
# DATA_BACKUP_PRUNE_DAYS=7
# DATA_BACKUPS_PATH=/srv/audiobookshelf-config/backups
# DATA_PATH=/config
# DATA_BACKUP_NAME=audiobookshelf-config-backup

# Resource limits (defaults shown). What moves these is scanning a large library
# and generating waveforms, not playback.
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_MEMORY_LIMIT=2g
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_CPU_LIMIT=2.0
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_MEMORY_RESERVATION=256m
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_CPU_RESERVATION=0.2
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_INIT_MEMORY_LIMIT=64m
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_INIT_CPU_LIMIT=0.5
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_INIT_MEMORY_RESERVATION=8m
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_INIT_CPU_RESERVATION=0.1
# TRAEFIK_MEMORY_LIMIT=256m
# TRAEFIK_CPU_LIMIT=0.5
# TRAEFIK_MEMORY_RESERVATION=64m
# TRAEFIK_CPU_RESERVATION=0.1
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_BACKUPS_MEMORY_LIMIT=256m
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_BACKUPS_CPU_LIMIT=0.5
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_BACKUPS_MEMORY_RESERVATION=16m
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_BACKUPS_CPU_RESERVATION=0.1

# How long docker waits before SIGKILL. The config directory holds a SQLite
# database that is written on every position update.
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_STOP_GRACE_PERIOD=60s

# Image versions. Every image is pinned by digest inside the compose file
# (x-images block); set the matching variable here to run a different version
# of that one image while every other pin stays as tested. Needs Docker
# Compose v2.5 or newer (2022).
# TRAEFIK_IMAGE_VERSION=3.7
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_IMAGE_VERSION=2.36.0
# AUDIOBOOKSHELF_BACKUPS_IMAGE_VERSION=3.22
